  "question": {
    "text": "A double ordinate $\\mathrm{PQ}$ of the hyperbola $\\frac{\\mathrm{x}^{2}}{\\mathrm{a}^{2}}-\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^{2}}{\\mathrm{~b}^{2}}=1$ is such that $\\Delta \\mathrm{OPQ}$ is equilateral, $\\mathrm{O}$ being the centre of the hyperbola. Then the eccentricity e satisfies the relation"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$1    < \\mathrm{e} < \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}>\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint:\r\n$P \\equiv(a \\sec \\theta, b \\tan \\theta) \\angle \\mathrm{POM}=\\tan 30^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{b}}{\\mathrm{a}} \\sin \\theta$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin \\theta=\\frac{a}{b \\sqrt{3}}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{b^{2}}{a^{2}}>\\frac{1}{3} \\quad \\Rightarrow 1+\\frac{b^{2}}{a^{2}}>\\frac{4}{3} \\quad \\Rightarrow e>\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0008_a653b993560f.png\">"
  }
}